    "content": "Watkins, Vernon (04/09/xxxx) \n### **Medical Progress Note**\n**Course of Stay:** Day 4 \n<columns>\n\t<column ratio=\"93.75\">\n\t\t<columns>\n\t\t\t<column ratio=\"37.5\">\n\t\t\t\t**Patient Name:** Vernon Watkins\n\t\t\t\t**Chief Complaint:** Nausea, vomiting and severe abdominal pain\n\t\t\t</column>\n\t\t\t<column ratio=\"29.17\">\n\t\t\t\t**DOB:** 04/09/XXXX\n\t\t\t\t**Physician:** Dr. Jack Nelson \n\t\t\t</column>\n\t\t\t<column ratio=\"33.33\">\n\t\t\t\t**Age/Sex:** 69-year-old male\n\t\t\t\t**Source of History:** Patient \n\t\t\t</column>\n\t\t</columns>\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"6.25\">\n\t</column>\n</columns>\n### **History of Present Illness**\nMr. Watkin presented to the ER 4 days agp with complaints of nausea, vomiting, and severe abdominal pain x 2 days.  Emergency hemicolectomy was performed and admitted to MS unit.\n<columns>\n\t<column ratio=\"25\">\n\t\t### **Past Medical History**\n\t\t- No history of surgeries \n\t\t- History of Hypertension, cataracts\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"25\">\n\t\t### **Family History**\n\t\t- None\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"25\">\n\t\t### **Allergies**\n\t\t- Penicillin\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"25\">\n\t\t### **Social History**\n\t\t- Lives with wife\n\t\t- Retired Postal Worker\n\t\t- Catholic\n\t\t- Smokes 1/2  pack day filtered 50 years\n\t</column>\n</columns>\n### **Assessment**\nVernon Watkins is a 69-year-old male with a history of hypertension who present to the ER with nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain x 2 days.  Upon arrival, the patient had abdomen was firm, distended and tender. Auscultation of the abdomen revealed hypoactive bowel sounds. Abdominal xray indicated perforated bowel with free fluid in abdomen.  Hemicolectomy was performed that day. Pt is current POD 4. Midline incision noted with no redness, swelling, or drainage. Bowel sounds are hypoactive and pt had bowel movement yesterday. Pt is frustrated and has refused to ambulate last night or this am. \n### **Plan**\n1. **Post Hemicolectomy**\n\t- Continue home meds\n\t- continue antibiotics\n2. **Diet:**\n\t- Regular\n3. **Oxygenation**:\n\t- titrate O2 to maintain SpO2\\>92%\nWatkins, Vernon (04/09/xxxx)"
