    "status": "released",
    "content": "###\n\n### **Postoperative Progress Note**\n**Patient Name:** Jane Fowler\n**DOB:** 01/28/XXXX\n**Age/Sex:** 79-year-old female\n**Date of Surgery:** Today\n**Surgeon:** Dr. Smith\n**Procedure:** **Total abdominal hysterectomy with bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy**\n---\n### **Subjective**\nPatient seen postoperatively and is awake, alert, and resting comfortably. She reports mild abdominal discomfort, which is currently well controlled. Denies nausea, vomiting, chest pain, or shortness of breath.\n---\n### **Objective**\nPatient is status post total abdominal hysterectomy with bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy performed under general anesthesia. The procedure was completed without intraoperative complications. Estimated blood loss was approximately 400 mL. Intraoperatively, two tumors were identified and removed, measuring 1.23 cm and 3.25 cm, respectively. The uterus, bilateral ovaries and fallopian tubes, tumors, and all associated surgical specimens were sent to pathology for evaluation.\nThe patient received 2 liters of Lactated Ringers intraoperatively, with IV Lactated Ringers currently infusing at 125 mL/hr. She was extubated in the operating room and is breathing spontaneously with stable vital signs. Abdominal incision is covered with a 4×4 gauze dressing that is clean, dry, and intact with no drainage noted. Indwelling urinary catheter remains in place with approximately 200 mL urine output documented postoperatively. Sequential compression devices are in place.\n---\n### **Assessment**\n79-year-old female status post uncomplicated **total abdominal hysterectomy with bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy** with removal of two tumors. Hemodynamically stable with appropriate urine output and no immediate postoperative complications identified.\n---\n### **Plan**\n1. **Postoperative Care**\n\t- Continue routine postoperative monitoring\n\t- Post-op vital signs per protocol\n2. **Fluids**\n\t- Continue **IV Lactated Ringers at 125 mL/hr**\n3. **Diet**\n\t- Sips of water; advance to clear liquids as tolerated\n4. **Pain Control**\n\t- **Morphine 2 mg IV push PRN pain**, may titrate up to **10 mg every 4 hours** as needed\n5. **Nausea**\n\t- **Zofran (Ondansetron) 4 mg IV push every 4 hours PRN**\n6. **Activity**\n\t- Out of bed this evening as tolerated\n7. **GU**\n\t- Maintain Foley catheter\n\t- Strict intake and output every 4 hours; notify provider for urine output \\<30 mL/hr\n8. **DVT Prophylaxis**\n\t- Continue sequential compression devices\n9. **Consults**\n\t- **Oncology consultation** requested\n10. **Pathology**\n- Await pathology results on surgical specimens\n\n- Transfer to surgical floor for continued postoperative care\n-"
