 Code","age":"16","sex":"Female","primaryDiagnosis":"Sickle Cell Crisis","barcode":"1004"},"chartRecords":[{"id":"chart-stephanie-smith-overview","patientId":"stephanie-smith","title":"Patient Overview","category":"summary","status":"released","content":"DOB:  07/14/XXXX\nAGE: 16 years old\nWT: 53.5 KG\nPrimary Diagnosis: Sickle Cell Crisis\n<span underline=\"true\">**Mother: Susan Smith 479-870-1225     Password: Milo**</span>\n\n<callout icon=\"✅\" color=\"blue_bg\">\n\tAllergies: NKDA\n</callout>\n\nA 16-year-old female patient was brought to the ED by her mother. She was diagnosed with sickle cell disease at the age of 5 and has been hospitalized annually for the past eight years due to crisis. The patient reports experiencing chest pain and shortness of breath. Her usual management with fluids, rest, and pain medication has been ineffective. She is currently alone in the room. In the ED, a type and crossmatch, along with a CBC, were drawn. Her mother provided consent for a blood transfusion.\n\n<columns>\n\t<column ratio=\"100\">\n\t\t# History\n\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"100\">\n\t\t# Physicians’ documents\n\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"100\">\n\t\t# Diagnostics\n\n\t</column>\n</columns>\n<columns>\n\t<column ratio=\"33.33\">\n\t\t# Nursing\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"41.67\">\n\t</column>\n\t<column ratio=\"25\">\n\t</column>\n</columns>"},{"id":"chart-256195d201d581178261f530c1cb52cc","patientId":"stephanie-smith","title":"Input and output tracking","category":"io","status":"released","content":"Intake/Output Flowchart\nUse this sheet to track how much your child takes in and how much comes out\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col width=\"69\">\n<col width=\"69\">\n<col width=\"69\">\n<col width=\"151\">\n<col width=\"132\">\n<col width=\"69\">\n<col width=\"140\">\n<col width=\"127\">\n<col width=\"124\">\n<col width=\"119\">\n</colgroup>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>**Intake**</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td>**Output**</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<