ble, normoactive in 4 quadrants; no reported/observed nausea, vomiting, diarrhea or constipation.\n\t<columns>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"18.75\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL\n\t\t</column>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"81.25\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL Except\n\t\t\tExceptions:\n\t\t</column>\n\t</columns>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Genitourinary</summary>\n\tWDL Definition: No reported or observed difficulties with voiding; urine reported or observed as clear, yellow and without foul odor\n\t<columns>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"18.75\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL\n\t\t</column>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"81.25\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL Except\n\t\t\tExceptions:\n\t\t</column>\n\t</columns>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Skin</summary>\n\tWDL Definition: Warm; dry; intact, elastic; without discoloration; pressure points without redness\n\t<columns>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"18.75\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL\n\t\t</column>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"81.25\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL Except\n\t\t\tExceptions:\n\t\t</column>\n\t</columns>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Musculoskeletal</summary>\n\tWDL Definition: No observed or reported muscle weakness, joint swelling or tenderness; all extremities with symmetrical movement bilaterally\n\t<columns>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"18.75\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL\n\t\t</column>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"81.25\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL Except\n\t\t\tExceptions:\n\t\t</column>\n\t</columns>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Peripheral neurovascular</summary>\n\tWDL Definition: Capillary refill less than/equal to 3 seconds; extremities warm with 2+ pulses; no discoloration or edema; no reported numbness, tingling, or tenderness\n\t<columns>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"18.75\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL\n\t\t</column>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"81.25\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL Except\n\t\t\tExceptions:\n\t\t</column>\n\t</columns>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Safety</summary>\n\tWDL Definition: bed in low position, wheels locked; call light in reach; upper side rails up x 2; ID band on\n\t<columns>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"18.75\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL\n\t\t</column>\n\t\t<column ratio=\"81.25\">\n\t\t\t- [ ] WDL Except\n\t\t\tExceptions:\n\t\t</column>\n\t</columns>\n</details>"},{"id":"chart-25d195d201d581a0a439ec5e6a8a85a4","patientId":"ruth-livingston","title":"ICU Orders","category":"orders","status":"released","content":"Livingston, Ruth (10/8/xxxx)\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col width=\"129\">\n<col width=\"427\">\n<col width=\"295.1999969482422\">\n</colgroup>\n<tr>\n<td>Date and time </td>\n<td>Order</td>\n<td>Type of order and who received the order  (Verbal/ Telephone)                                  Example : RBTO from Dr. Darnell/S, Escbobar ATUNS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>1. Transfer to ICU</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>2. Dx: Post-Op Open Reduction internal Fixation (ORIF)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td> 3. Diet: Regular</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>4. Code status: Full code </td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>5.  Activity: bed Rest </td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>6. continuous ECG and POX monitoring</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>7. Physical Therapy: Evaluate for passive ROM advance when able</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>8.  Administer Supplemental O2 to keep SpO2 \\>93%</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>9. Vital signs q 15 min and PRN; I&O q 4 hrs</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>10. Normal saline bolus 500 ml over 30 min stat </td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>11. After fluid bolus if MAP \\< 65  or SBP \\<100 start:                           Norepinephrine (Levophed) @ 2 mcg/min continuous IV, titrate by 2 mcg q 5 minutes to maintain MAP \\>65 or SBP \\>100. Maximum dose 30 mcg/min</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>11.  Place foley catheter </td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>12.. Sterile Dressing change to right hip q 12 hrs</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td>13. Labs: BMP, CBC, lactate level prior to starting IV antibiotics</td>\n<td></